   "text": "This is a camptothecin-type (exatecan-like) drug-linker: a maleimidocaproyl\u2013Gly\u2013Gly\u2013Phe\u2013Gly peptide linker joined through an NH\u2013CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2 spacer to the amino-fluoro camptothecin core.\n\n- **Maleimide end:** a 2,5-dioxopyrrole (maleimide) N-linked to a five-methylene chain ending in an amide carbonyl (6-maleimidohexanoyl).\n- **Peptide:** Gly\u2013Gly\u2013Phe\u2013Gly. The Phe \u03b1-carbon has its benzyl group on a hashed bond, which corresponds to L-Phe, so it is written `N[C@@H](Cc1ccccc1)C(=O)N`.\n- **Spacer:** the last Gly C=O is bonded to NH\u2013CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2, and that CH2 is attached to the quinoline carbon at the top of the core.\n- **Core:** the benzo ring carries NH2 and F. It is fused to the quinoline and then to the pyrrolo-fused pyridone and the lactone ring. The quaternary carbon bears OH (wedged bond), ethyl and the lactone C=O.\n- **Quaternary stereocentre:** I assigned `[C@@]` from the wedge geometry by working out the chirality sign by hand, and it agrees with the usual 20(S) camptothecin configuration.\n\nI checked the ring-closure labels by hand and they close correctly; I did not run the string through a parser.\n\nSMILES: O=C1C=CC(=O)N1CCCCCC(=O)NCC(=O)NCC(=O)N[C@@H](Cc1ccccc1)C(=O)NCC(=O)NCOCc4c5cc(N)c(F)cc5nc5c4CN4C(=O)c6c(cc54)[C@@](O)(CC)C(=O)OC6"
  }
